Subject: [PATCH] include: linux: types: add 128-bit integer types

The bundled linux/types.h shadows the toolchain's UAPI header and defines
the same include guard. ARM64 sigcontext.h from Linux 7.3.5 uses __u128,
so including sys/wait.h fails when the bundled header is used first.

Add the signed and unsigned 128-bit types with the same alignment and
compiler guard as the kernel UAPI header.

---
 include/linux/types.h | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/types.h b/include/linux/types.h
--- a/include/linux/types.h
+++ b/include/linux/types.h
@@ -6,6 +6,11 @@
 #ifndef __ASSEMBLY__
 
 #include <linux/posix_types.h>
 
+#ifdef __SIZEOF_INT128__
+typedef __signed__ __int128 __s128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+typedef unsigned __int128 __u128 __attribute__((aligned(16)));
+#endif
+
 
 /*
